{%- comment -%}
  Cart drawer — thin section wrapper.

  All of the markup lives in snippets/ness-cart-drawer.liquid. This file exists
  so the drawer is addressable by the Section Rendering API: ness-cart.js calls
  `/?sections=ness-cart-drawer` after every cart mutation and swaps the returned
  [data-cart-content] into the live drawer. That keeps the Liquid as the single
  source of truth for the drawer's markup — no line item is ever assembled in
  JavaScript, so prices, discounts, and line item properties can only ever be
  what Shopify rendered.

  Rendered once per page by layout/theme.liquid with a static {% section %} tag.
  It has no presets and no settings, so it cannot be added, removed, or
  reordered from the customizer — see PLAN.md, Editability policy, where the
  cart overlay is listed as "editable: nothing".

  The stylesheet and script tags come back in every Section Rendering API
  response too, but the script only ever reads [data-cart-content] out of that
  response, so they are discarded rather than accumulating in the document.
{%- endcomment -%}

{{ 'ness-cart.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
<script src="{{ 'ness-cart.js' | asset_url }}" defer="defer"></script>

{%- render 'ness-cart-drawer' -%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Cart drawer",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "The cart drawer has nothing to configure. Everything in it — products, quantities, prices, discounts, and the Processing Time and Pickup Option chosen on the product page — comes from Shopify and from what the shopper picked."
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
